IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa19-nouns`
IMPORT `coa19-a1-delivery`

-- coa19-tests-a1-delivery.l4: tests for coa19-a1-delivery.l4 (ss 859A to 859G).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the section named in the comment above it, not from the code's output.
-- Day counts: "21 days beginning with the day after X" ends on X plus 21 (day 1 is the day after X).

§ `Tests: ss 859A to 859G`

§§ `s 859A(7) definitions`
-- "cash" includes foreign currency: foreign currency is cash; any other money is not decided ("includes").
#ASSERT `s 859A(7) the money is cash` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859A(7) the money is cash` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "charge" includes (a) a mortgage; (b) a Scots right in security, "but not including a pledge".
#ASSERT `s 859A(7) the arrangement is a charge` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859A(7) the arrangement is a charge` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859A(7) the arrangement is a charge` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859A(7) the arrangement is a charge` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A pledge that is not a Scots right in security: the exclusion is in paragraph (b) only, so the text does not decide.
#ASSERT `s 859A(7) the arrangement is a charge` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "company" means a UK-registered company.
#ASSERT `s 859A(7) the body is a company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859A(7) the body is a company` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 859A(6) and (1)`
`s 859A test: no exclusion` MEANS `s 859A(6) the charge` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 859A test: landlord's cash deposit` MEANS `s 859A(6) the charge` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 859A test: Lloyd's underwriting` MEANS `s 859A(6) the charge` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s 859A test: excluded by another Act` MEANS `s 859A(6) the charge` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

-- (6) "This section does not apply to" the three kinds: each is excluded; any other charge is not decided by (6).
#ASSERT `s 859A(6) the charge is excluded from the application of section 859A` `s 859A test: landlord's cash deposit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859A(6) the charge is excluded from the application of section 859A` `s 859A test: Lloyd's underwriting` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859A(6) the charge is excluded from the application of section 859A` `s 859A test: excluded by another Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859A(6) the charge is excluded from the application of section 859A` `s 859A test: no exclusion` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) applies where a company creates a charge, subject to (6).
#ASSERT `s 859A(1) this section applies` TRUE TRUE `s 859A test: no exclusion` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859A(1) this section applies` FALSE TRUE `s 859A test: no exclusion` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859A(1) this section applies` TRUE FALSE `s 859A test: no exclusion` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859A(1) this section applies` TRUE TRUE `s 859A test: landlord's cash deposit` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859A(1) this section applies` TRUE TRUE `s 859A test: Lloyd's underwriting` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859A(1) this section applies` TRUE TRUE `s 859A test: excluded by another Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 859A(4) the period allowed for delivery`
-- 21 days beginning with the day after the date of creation: 1 January 2025 gives 22 January 2025.
#ASSERT `s 859A(4) the last day of the period allowed for delivery` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING EQUALS Date 22 1 2025
-- across a month end, a year end and both kinds of February
#ASSERT `s 859A(4) the last day of the period allowed for delivery` (Date 20 1 2025) NOTHING EQUALS Date 10 2 2025
#ASSERT `s 859A(4) the last day of the period allowed for delivery` (Date 20 12 2024) NOTHING EQUALS Date 10 1 2025
#ASSERT `s 859A(4) the last day of the period allowed for delivery` (Date 15 2 2024) NOTHING EQUALS Date 7 3 2024
#ASSERT `s 859A(4) the last day of the period allowed for delivery` (Date 15 2 2025) NOTHING EQUALS Date 8 3 2025
-- "unless an order allowing an extended period is made under section 859F(3)": the order's last day governs.
#ASSERT `s 859A(4) the last day of the period allowed for delivery` (Date 1 1 2025) (JUST (Date 30 4 2025)) EQUALS Date 30 4 2025

§§ `s 859A(2), (3), (5) and the three read together`
-- (2): the registrar must register if, before the end of the period, the company or a person interested delivers a section 859D statement.
#ASSERT `s 859A(2) the registrar must register the charge` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 22 1 2025) (Date 22 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859A(2) the registrar must register the charge` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 22 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859A(2) the registrar must register the charge` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 23 1 2025) (Date 22 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859A(2) the registrar must register the charge` FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 22 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859A(2) the registrar must register the charge` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 22 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859A(2) the registrar must register the charge` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 22 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3): where the charge is created or evidenced by an instrument, required only if a certified copy is delivered.
#ASSERT `s 859A(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859A(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859A(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859A(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): where an order is made under 859F(3) a copy of the order must be delivered with the statement.
#ASSERT `s 859A(5) a copy of the order must be delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859A(5) a copy of the order must be delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2), (3) and (5) together.
#ASSERT `s 859A(2) to (5) the registrar is required to register the charge` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859A(2) to (5) the registrar is required to register the charge` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859A(2) to (5) the registrar is required to register the charge` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859A(2) to (5) the registrar is required to register the charge` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an order was made and its copy was not delivered: the text does not say what follows (subsection (5) has no "only if")
#ASSERT `s 859A(2) to (5) the registrar is required to register the charge` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859A(2) to (5) the registrar is required to register the charge` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 859B Charge in series of debentures`
-- (1): all of (a) and (b) hold and the instruments are debentures (s 738, a seam).
#ASSERT `s 859B(1) this section applies` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859B(1) this section applies` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(1) this section applies` NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859B(1) this section applies` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(1) this section applies` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(1) this section applies` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (6): 21 days beginning with the day after the deed is executed, or if no deed after the first debenture is executed.
#ASSERT `s 859B(6) the last day of the period allowed for delivery` TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 10 3 2025) EQUALS Date 22 3 2025
#ASSERT `s 859B(6) the last day of the period allowed for delivery` FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 10 3 2025) EQUALS Date 31 3 2025
-- (8) "deed" means (a) or (b).
#ASSERT `s 859B(8) the instrument is a deed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859B(8) the instrument is a deed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859B(8) the instrument is a deed` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2)(a)-(c): trustees named (each, or any four of more than four with a statement that there are others), resolution dates,
-- and the covering instrument's date if there is one.
#ASSERT `s 859B(2)(a) to (c) the statement contains the further particulars` 3 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2)(a) to (c) the statement contains the further particulars` 6 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2)(a) to (c) the statement contains the further particulars` 6 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2)(a) to (c) the statement contains the further particulars` 4 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2)(a) to (c) the statement contains the further particulars` 3 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2)(a) to (c) the statement contains the further particulars` 3 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2)(a) to (c) the statement contains the further particulars` 3 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (2): the duty, with the deadline.
#ASSERT `s 859B(2) the registrar must register the charge` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (Date 22 3 2025) (Date 22 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2) the registrar must register the charge` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (Date 23 3 2025) (Date 22 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2) the registrar must register the charge` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 22 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2) the registrar must register the charge` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 22 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2) the registrar must register the charge` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 22 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2) the registrar must register the charge` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 22 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2) the registrar must register the charge` NOTHING TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 22 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3), (4): only if the certified copy of the instrument (or, with no instrument, of one of the debentures) is delivered.
#ASSERT `s 859B(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859B(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859B(4) the registrar is required to register the charge` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(4) the registrar is required to register the charge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859B(4) the registrar is required to register the charge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): taken to be a section 859D statement even without the names of the debenture holders.
#ASSERT `s 859B(5) the statement is taken to be a section 859D statement of particulars` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 859B(5) the statement is taken to be a section 859D statement of particulars` FALSE)
-- (7) as (5) of s 859A.
#ASSERT `s 859B(7) a copy of the order must be delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859B(7) a copy of the order must be delivered to the registrar with the statement of particulars` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2), (3), (4), (7) together
#ASSERT `s 859B(2) to (7) the registrar is required to register the charge` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2) to (7) the registrar is required to register the charge` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2) to (7) the registrar is required to register the charge` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2) to (7) the registrar is required to register the charge` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2) to (7) the registrar is required to register the charge` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859B(2) to (7) the registrar is required to register the charge` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859B(2) to (7) the registrar is required to register the charge` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 859C Charges existing on property or undertaking acquired`
-- (1): where a company acquires property or undertaking subject to a charge of a kind capable of being registered under s 859A.
#ASSERT `s 859C(1) this section applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 859A test: no exclusion` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859C(1) this section applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE `s 859A test: no exclusion` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859C(1) this section applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 859A test: no exclusion` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859C(1) this section applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE `s 859A test: no exclusion` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859C(1) this section applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 859A test: landlord's cash deposit` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859C(1) this section applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 859A test: Lloyd's underwriting` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): the registrar must register if the company or a person interested delivers a section 859D statement (no time limit in (2)).
#ASSERT `s 859C(2) the registrar must register the charge` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859C(2) the registrar must register the charge` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859C(2) the registrar must register the charge` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859C(2) the registrar must register the charge` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859C(2) the registrar must register the charge` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) and (2) with (3)
#ASSERT `s 859C(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859C(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859C(3) the registrar is required to register the charge` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859C(2) and (3) the registrar is required to register the charge` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859C(2) and (3) the registrar is required to register the charge` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859C(2) and (3) the registrar is required to register the charge` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859C(2) and (3) the registrar is required to register the charge` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 859D Particulars to be delivered to registrar`
-- the 14 particulars, in the order of the DECLARE:
--   name&number, date of creation, date of acquisition, names (i), four names + others (ii), floating, further security, land etc.,
--   other fixed security, (3)(a) no instrument, (3)(b) names, nature, description, obligations
`s 859D test: instrument, complete` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 859D test: instrument, complete with the date of acquisition` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 859D test: instrument, four names and a statement of others` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 859D test: instrument, no names` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 859D test: instrument, no company name and number` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 859D test: instrument, no date of creation` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 859D test: instrument, no floating charge particular` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 859D test: instrument, no further security particular` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 859D test: instrument, no land ship aircraft particular` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 859D test: instrument, no other fixed security particular` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 859D test: no instrument, complete` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s 859D test: no instrument, no statement that there is no instrument` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s 859D test: no instrument, no names` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s 859D test: no instrument, no nature` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`s 859D test: no instrument, no description` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s 859D test: no instrument, no obligations` MEANS `s 859D what the statement contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

-- (2): the particulars for an instrument; "(ii) where there are more than four such persons ... the names of any four": 5 persons is more than four, 4 is not.
#ASSERT `s 859D(2) the particulars listed in subsection (2) are contained` `s 859D test: instrument, complete` 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859D(2) the particulars listed in subsection (2) are contained` `s 859D test: instrument, four names and a statement of others` 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859D(2) the particulars listed in subsection (2) are contained` `s 859D test: instrument, four names and a statement of others` 4 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859D(2) the particulars listed in subsection (2) are contained` `s 859D test: instrument, no names` 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859D(2) the particulars listed in subsection (2) are contained` `s 859D test: instrument, no floating charge particular` 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859D(2) the particulars listed in subsection (2) are contained` `s 859D test: instrument, no further security particular` 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859D(2) the particulars listed in subsection (2) are contained` `s 859D test: instrument, no land ship aircraft particular` 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859D(2) the particulars listed in subsection (2) are contained` `s 859D test: instrument, no other fixed security particular` 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3): the particulars where there is no instrument
#ASSERT `s 859D(3) the particulars listed in subsection (3) are contained` `s 859D test: no instrument, complete` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859D(3) the particulars listed in subsection (3) are contained` `s 859D test: no instrument, no statement that there is no instrument` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859D(3) the particulars listed in subsection (3) are contained` `s 859D test: no instrument, no names` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859D(3) the particulars listed in subsection (3) are contained` `s 859D test: no instrument, no nature` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859D(3) the particulars listed in subsection (3) are contained` `s 859D test: no instrument, no description` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859D(3) the particulars listed in subsection (3) are contained` `s 859D test: no instrument, no obligations` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1): a statement of particulars is a section 859D statement if it contains (a), (b) and (c) or (d)
#ASSERT `s 859D(1) the statement is a section 859D statement of particulars` `s 859D test: instrument, complete` 2 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859D(1) the statement is a section 859D statement of particulars` `s 859D test: instrument, no company name and number` 2 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859D(1) the statement is a section 859D statement of particulars` `s 859D test: instrument, no date of creation` 2 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859D(1) the statement is a section 859D statement of particulars` `s 859D test: instrument, no names` 2 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1)(b): for a charge to which s 859C applies the date of acquisition is also needed
#ASSERT `s 859D(1) the statement is a section 859D statement of particulars` `s 859D test: instrument, complete` 2 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859D(1) the statement is a section 859D statement of particulars` `s 859D test: instrument, complete with the date of acquisition` 2 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1)(d): no instrument
#ASSERT `s 859D(1) the statement is a section 859D statement of particulars` `s 859D test: no instrument, complete` 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859D(1) the statement is a section 859D statement of particulars` `s 859D test: no instrument, no nature` 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a statement for a charge with no instrument must not be judged by the instrument list
#ASSERT `s 859D(1) the statement is a section 859D statement of particulars` `s 859D test: instrument, complete` 2 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the helper behind s 859B(5): everything but the names
#ASSERT `s 859D(1) the statement lacks nothing but possibly the names of the persons in whose favour the charge has been created` `s 859D test: instrument, no names` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859D(1) the statement lacks nothing but possibly the names of the persons in whose favour the charge has been created` `s 859D test: instrument, complete` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 859D(1) the statement lacks nothing but possibly the names of the persons in whose favour the charge has been created` `s 859D test: instrument, no floating charge particular` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 859D(1) the statement lacks nothing but possibly the names of the persons in whose favour the charge has been created` `s 859D test: instrument, no company name and number` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT `s 859D(1) the statement lacks nothing but possibly the names of the persons in whose favour the charge has been created` `s 859D test: no instrument, complete` FALSE FALSE
-- (4) fixed security: the Companies Act 1985 is outside the sources; the borrowed answer is an input
#ASSERT `s 859D(4) the arrangement is fixed security` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859D(4) the arrangement is fixed security` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859D(4) the arrangement is fixed security` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5) intellectual property includes patents etc. and licences
#ASSERT `s 859D(5) the right is intellectual property` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859D(5) the right is intellectual property` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859D(5) the right is intellectual property` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 859E Date of creation of charge`
-- (1) Table, row by row: the date is the date of the event column 2 names.
#ASSERT `s 859E(1) the date on which the charge is taken to be created` `s 859E a standard security` (Date 5 6 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 5 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 859E(1) the date on which the charge is taken to be created` `s 859E a charge created or evidenced by a deed that has been executed and has immediate effect on execution and delivery` (Date 6 6 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 6 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 859E(1) the date on which the charge is taken to be created` `s 859E a charge created or evidenced by a deed that has been executed and held in escrow` (Date 7 6 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 7 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 859E(1) the date on which the charge is taken to be created` `s 859E a charge created or evidenced by a deed that has been executed and held as undelivered` (Date 8 6 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 8 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 859E(1) the date on which the charge is taken to be created` `s 859E a charge created or evidenced by an instrument that is not a deed and has immediate effect on execution` (Date 9 6 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 9 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 859E(1) the date on which the charge is taken to be created` `s 859E a charge created or evidenced by an instrument that is not a deed and does not have immediate effect on execution` (Date 10 6 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 859E(1) the date on which the charge is taken to be created` `s 859E a charge not created or evidenced by an instrument` (Date 11 6 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 11 6 2025)
-- a charge the Table does not describe has no date in the Table
#ASSERT `s 859E(1) the date on which the charge is taken to be created` `s 859E a charge the Table does not describe` (Date 11 6 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) execution by all the parties whose execution is essential: the date is the last of their dates
#ASSERT `s 859E(2) the date of execution of an instrument made between two or more parties` TRUE (LIST Date 10 1 2025, Date 12 1 2025, Date 11 1 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 12 1 2025)
#ASSERT `s 859E(2) the date of execution of an instrument made between two or more parties` TRUE (LIST Date 3 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 3 3 2025)
#ASSERT `s 859E(2) the date of execution of an instrument made between two or more parties` FALSE (LIST Date 10 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859E(2) the date of execution of an instrument made between two or more parties` TRUE EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) applies even if further steps are necessary for other purposes
#ASSERT `s 859E(3) the date of creation in this section applies for the purposes of Chapter A1` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859E(3) the date of creation in this section applies for the purposes of Chapter A1` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (4) the registrar may accept the date given in a section 859D statement
#ASSERT `s 859E(4) the registrar is entitled without further enquiry to accept the charge as created on that date` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859E(4) the registrar is entitled without further enquiry to accept the charge as created on that date` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5) "deed" means (a) or (b)
#ASSERT `s 859E(5) the instrument is a deed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859E(5) the instrument is a deed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859E(5) the instrument is a deed` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (6) delivery includes delivery as a deed where required
#ASSERT `s 859E(6) a reference to delivery of the deed is satisfied` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859E(6) a reference to delivery of the deed is satisfied` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 859F Extension of period allowed for delivery`
-- (2) the requirement: (a)(i) or (a)(ii) or (b)
#ASSERT `s 859F(2) the requirement is met` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859F(2) the requirement is met` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859F(2) the requirement is met` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859F(2) the requirement is met` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1) subsection (3) applies if the court is satisfied that no one delivered in time and the requirement is met
#ASSERT `s 859F(1) subsection (3) applies` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859F(1) subsection (3) applies` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859F(1) subsection (3) applies` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3) the court may extend, on the application of the company or a person interested
#ASSERT `s 859F(3) the court may order that the period allowed for delivery be extended` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859F(3) the court may order that the period allowed for delivery be extended` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 859F(3) the court may order that the period allowed for delivery be extended` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE; s 859F(3): the power is given on the gate quoted and the text does not say the person has none otherwise, so NOTHING (name-test sweep: a grant is not turned into a bar)
#ASSERT `s 859F(3) the court may order that the period allowed for delivery be extended` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859F(3) the court may order that the period allowed for delivery be extended` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 859G Personal information etc in certified copies`
-- (1) the three kinds are not required; the name of an individual and any other item are not decided
#ASSERT `s 859G(1) the item is required to be included in a certified copy of an instrument or debenture` `s 859G personal information relating to an individual, other than the name of an individual` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859G(1) the item is required to be included in a certified copy of an instrument or debenture` `s 859G the number or other identifier of a bank or securities account of a company or individual` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859G(1) the item is required to be included in a certified copy of an instrument or debenture` `s 859G a signature` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859G(1) the item is required to be included in a certified copy of an instrument or debenture` `s 859G the name of an individual` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859G(1) the item is required to be included in a certified copy of an instrument or debenture` `s 859G any other item` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) the registrar may accept the certified copy whether or not any of that information is in it
#ASSERT `s 859G(2) the registrar is entitled without further enquiry to accept the certified copy of the instrument` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859G(2) the registrar is entitled without further enquiry to accept the certified copy of the instrument` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859G(2) the registrar is entitled without further enquiry to accept the certified copy of the instrument` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
